A||||64||TRiAD||"The only American-mad Mid-engined car" (not!)||||4||
Z||000000||TRiAD||12-29-2001||03:20 AM||||OK, this irks me. I keep seeing people billing the fiero as "The only American-made Mid-engined car", or something very similar. <P>This is simply NOT the case!<P>IF you stick to "production" cars; <P>1) The Vector W2 Twin Turbo (W8 Twin Turbo Prototype) was the FIRST (there were actually VERY few made). <P>2) The Fiero was the second<P>3) The Vector W8 Twin Turbo, and M12 (although the M12 was not a "real" Vector) are on the list<P>4) And Mosler has had SEVERAL, including the current MT900. <P>5) Saleen now has the S7 and S7R as well. <P>I know it's not an intentionally misleading statement, but I thought it time to shed some light on the subject, since the information is in fact incorrect. <P>Thanks for listening.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">  <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Devotshka||12-29-2001||03:25 AM||||Ya know which one bugs me i've seen like 3 times this week?  The "best american made mid-engine two seat GM car made from 1984-1988"  <BR>Crapola, they made others?!?  Could ya get a little more precise??||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||12-29-2001||03:32 AM||||Only one ever made in any kind of volume?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How about in enough volume to be considered a  'production line' automobile?<P>Enough to need full emmisions testing?<P>Add to the short list:<P>(sort of.) the DeLorean.<P>and the Pantera.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Blacktree||12-29-2001||03:47 AM||||Wasn't the Corvair a mid-engine car? Oh, wait a minute... the Corvair was rear-engine. Never mind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||12-29-2001||08:08 AM||||How about "the <B>ONLY</B> American-made mid-engine car <B>THAT DOESN'T COST AS MUCH AS A FRICKIN' THREE-BEDROOM HOUSE</B>"...||||reg||1
Z||000005||kyote||12-29-2001||08:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B><P>IF you stick to "production" cars; <P>1) The Vector W2 Twin Turbo <P>3) The Vector W8 Twin Turbo, and M12 <P>4) And Mosler has had SEVERAL, including the current MT900. <P>5) Saleen now has the S7 and S7R as well. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So who makes No.'s 1,3,4 & 5..??<BR>and in what numbers..?<BR>In order to be considered a "production car"<BR>there is a minimum number of vehicles that have to be made per year to qualify..<BR>Just having 10 to 100 or so a year does not qualify a car to be a "production car"<BR>Now I may be an "Old Fogey"..<BR>But I have never heard of any of the others..<P>Just my .02 worth.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||12-29-2001||08:36 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Only one ever made in any kind of volume?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How about in enough volume to be considered a  'production line' automobile?<P>Enough to need full emmisions testing?<P>Add to the short list:<P>(sort of.) the DeLorean.<P>and the Pantera.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought we were talking about American made cars.<P>DeLorean - Ireland<BR>Pantera - Italy<P>Both were sold through Ford/Lincoln dealerships and the Pantera used Ford engines, but they were foreign cars.  <P>EDIT:  Oops!  DeLoreans were sold through GM dealers, not Ford.  They were built in Ireland though.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
