Z||000008||TRiAD||12-29-2001||10:30 AM||||Thanks Wampus, ecactly right. <P>Now, sone people make dinstinctions like "low numbers aren't production" and "if it's not off an assembly line, it's not production", but the government doesn't. <P>All these cars had to pass emisisons testing, as well. <P>Every one of the cars I posted is/was in series production, most on assembly lines (except the Vector W2/W8, they're more hand-crafted than the rest, and were made in one spot by a "team"). <P>Yes, most of these were/are expensive, but the people saying "America's ONLY mid-engined car" said nothing about it being the only "affordable" car. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||4BanGinFun||12-29-2001||12:18 PM||||"America's/Canada's ONLY affordable mid-engined car"<P>that better   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P>  &lt;A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/<BR>" TARGET=_blank&gt;www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/<BR>&lt;/A&gt;    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/minifiero1.gif">    <BR>far future plans.<p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||6
