Z||000027||gargoyle||12-29-2001||08:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85 gt fiero:<BR><B>The fiero was the FIRST AMERICAN MADE SPORTS CAR.!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK, this is definitely wrong. The Fiero was initially introduced as a two seat commuter car NOT a sports car. This car would have never been allowed to occur if it would have been introduced as a "sports car". Nothing shall be allowed to threaten the sacred fiberglass boat known as the Corvette.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||BN Boomer||12-29-2001||08:44 PM||||Okay, how about this:<P>"The Fiero, America's only successful mid-engine car"<P>Being as the Fiero is the only automobile of the qualifiers mentioned thus far to have been produced in significant numbers over an appreciable number of years, I think this is an apt and fitting description. <P>The Fiero was cancelled simply because it was not generating a high enough profit margin for GM and they felt their reources were better used on programs the offered a more favorable return on investment. How many of the other automobiles mentioned were discontinued because they weren't turning any profit whatsoever and in fact were likely losing money? My guess is all of them.<P>Even now, I'll bet GM could bring back a Fiero true to it's origins but with technological updates and make a buck or two in the process. I do not feel that they would ever put forth the effort necesary to achieve that, but it could be done.||||reg||1
