Z||000059||BN Boomer||12-31-2001||09:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by soup:<BR><B>learn to respect the opinions of others.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Isn't that a two way street? If someone wants to refer to their Fiero as "America's only mid-engine car", why should they have to worry about Triad sicking his attorney on them? <P>Is Pontiac really driving excitement?<P>Is Chevrolet really the Heartbeat of America?<P>Is the Silverado really like a rock?<P>Is Nissan really driven?<P>What's the big farkin' deal?<P>Come on, people, inquiring minds want to know!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000060||firstfiero||12-31-2001||10:31 AM||||    I'm supposed to respect the opp. of others when the other...Triad... Doesn't respect mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> I only respect someone when they give it in return. Triads usually pretty cool but on this thread he's acted like an A$$. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000061||TRiAD||12-31-2001||11:02 AM||||Boomer, I never said anything about sicking an attournet on anyone. All I said was that this particular statement is a statement of provable facts, not opinion, and that incorrect facts could get someone eventually into trouble. It was really meant as more of a public service than anything. Sorry for trying to help. <P>firstfiero and anyone else who feels that way, I'm sorry. I didn't realise I was "acting like an a$$". <P>There are many things in this world where "opinions" are all we have. There's no problem with that, and I feel I give people plenty room for theirs in those conversations. We may discuss the differences of them, but I feel there can be mutual respect on those occasions. <BR>There are other situations where there is a provable fact of the matter, and this always negates opinions. If we all stand around stating our opinions, and the truth comes out, our opinions don't matter. Yours, mine, anyone's. <P>The simple fact is that the statement is not trthful. The fact that others want to continue calling their car something it's not I guess is no big deal. I just wanted to shed some light on the subject. <P>I never thought the difference between a fact and an opinion would be so elusive. I'm sorry if anyone's ego was hurt, that was not the intention. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000062||Turbo88||12-31-2001||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadero2dmax:<BR><B> None of the mentioned vehicles were ever meant to be on the streets of Tulsa, OK<BR>Seems like the cold weather and snows have put a lot of people inside, where they can play "what if" about Fieros on their computers!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah, but the only cars ment for the streets of Tulsa Oklahoma are SUVs and pickups. This is because they are the only vehicles which can manage the roads here without a 4 wheel alignment every 6 months!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000063||NEPTUNE||12-31-2001||12:16 PM||||In 1963 Ford built 6 Mustang I concept cars. Looked like a small 2M4 Targa.<BR>These mid engined cars were powered by a German Ford Taurus engine (V4)and transmission borrowed from the front drive sedan. There never was any plan to mass produce them, as Ford knew the market for this type of car was very limited. Hence the Falcon based mustang. <p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000064||Mickey_Moose||12-31-2001||12:55 PM||||technically any car made in Canada or Mexico can still be called made in America (North America)...vs parts made in Europe, Japan, Germany, or whatever...<P>flame war &gt;&gt; any time anyone posts anything in the tone that was originally posted, it is meant as a flame war...<P>Tucker &gt;&gt; movies have a tendency to distort facts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If the US government states that the S7 and Vector are production cars...fine...I NEVER said they were not (maybe I implied it??), but then I also never said the Fiero was the only American made one either...to be quite honest, there have been several mid engine cars made in the US - it's just stupid arguing the point about the S7 or Vector. For someone who is so bent on the S7, fine...but remember you still can't compare the S7 to any other car made (if you must, please compare it to other cars in it's class like the McLaren F1) (besides, no one is stopping you from owning one).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Let people live in their own little worlds - and if they get sued over something, then they will learn...(hopefully)...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
